Experiment 1: Information gathering using google, learning techniques of google Search Engine
Theory
Google dorking is the use of advanced google search operators to find specific information from publicly indexed web pages. 
It helps in passive information gathering because it does not directly interact with target system.
Google Search Operators
Site: Restricts search results to a specific website or domain
  Example: (i) Site: wikipedia.org artificial intelligence - searches for artificial intelligence only on wikipedia
  (ii) Site: gov.in cyber security - searches for cybersecurity only on Indian government websites
Intitle: - Searches for word or exact phrase in the webpage title
  Example: intitle: "index of" "parent directory" - search for pages with "index of" in the title and "parent directory" in the page content
Allintitle - Searches for pages whose titles contains all the specific words
  Example: (i) allintitle: annual report 2025 - searches for pages whose title contains annual, report & 2025
inurl - Searches for a word or phrase within the webpage url
  Example (i) inurl: admin site: _.in - find .in websites whose URL's contain the word admin
  (ii) inurl: login site: edu - finds educational websites where URL contains word login
allinurl: - Searches for URL's containing all the specified words
  Example: (i) allinurl: wp content uploads, searches for URL's containing both wp-content and uploadintext: searches a specific word or phrase within the body of webpages
  Eg) site: _.gov filetype: pdf intext: "budget" - finds government pdf documents containing the word "budget"
  (ii) intext: "cyber security" site: edu - finds educational website containing the phrase "cyber security"
allintext: searches for webpage containing all specific words in their body text
  Eg: (i) allintext: cyber security awareness - finds pages whose body text contains cyber, security, awareness- : - Excludes a specified word from search results
  Eg) (i) Python -snake - searches for Python while excluding results related to snake
related: Finds websites related or similar to a specified URL
  Eg) (i) related: wikipedia.org (ii) related: github.com
